Improvement: The "Mean Reversion" Check
In your trend_cache.py, you currently track price_vs_vwap. A simple way to avoid peaks is to monitor the Distance from VWAP or the EMA20.
The Logic: If the price is more than X% away from the EMA20, it is "overextended".
The Action: Even if is_bullish is true, block the entry until the price pulls back closer to the moving average.
You could update your TrendData or SignalGenerator to store the local_high and local_low for the last n candles:
  # Conceptual check for _check_entry_conditions
  if current_price >= local_high * 0.998:  # Price is within 0.2% of local high
      return False, "Too close to local peak/resistance"

